    "finalContents": [
      "{\"summary\":\"Reviewed the four changed files. The test addition is consistent with the new timezone/date-override behavior. However, the implementation in packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/slots.ts introduces a concrete availability regression in working-hours filtering: the code computes both start and end minute values from the slot start time, so slots that extend past working-hours end are not rejected. I did not find additional supported bugs in the other changed files.\",\"fileVerdicts\":[{\"path\":\"apps/web/test/lib/getSchedule.test.ts\",\"verdict\":\"clean\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lib/slots.ts\",\"verdict\":\"clean\"},{\"path\":\"packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/slots.ts\",\"verdict\":\"buggy\"},{\"path\":\"packages/types/schedule.d.ts\",\"verdict\":\"clean\"}],\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Working-hours check ignores the slot end time\",\"claim\":\"The new working-hours filter computes both `start` and `end` from `slotStartTime`, so it never checks whether the slot extends beyond `workingHour.endTime`. As a result, a slot that starts inside working hours but ends after them can still be treated as available.\",\"path\":\"packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/slots.ts\",\"startLine\":132,\"endLine\":136}]}"
    ],
